---
import ConceptIndex from "../../components/ConceptIndex.astro";
import { foundationsDocs } from "../../data/foundations";
---

<ConceptIndex
  section="Foundations"
  heading="Before you"
  emphasis="build anything."
  description="The core model behind every watershed document: typed schemas, channel topology, and startup."
  scope="Core · every watershed app"
  docs={foundationsDocs}
  base="/foundations"
  ledgerIntro={`${foundationsDocs.length} sheets. Read in order — each one leans on the last.`}
>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    <p class="lede">
      The <a href="/guide">build guide</a> walks a working board through every
      step. These sheets cover the model underneath it: how you declare and lay
      out a document, and how you bring its channels online.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">
      Building a screen users can assemble for themselves? That optional layer
      now has its own section: <a href="/component-model">the component model</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <p slot="aside">
    Once a channel exists, <a href="/structures">the field atlas</a> covers what
    it does when two clients touch it at once, and <a href="/runtime">runtime</a>
    covers what happens while it's live: optimistic edits, reconnect, and the
    rest. Ready to see it running? Start <a href="/guide">the survey procedure</a>
    at step one.
  </p>
</ConceptIndex>
